The .panel has `overflow-y:auto` and max-height 94vh, so it scrolls internally; the screenshot shows a scrollbar on the panel. The START button is below. On a real mobile user can scroll. Acceptable, but better to fit everything with reduced typography. Add in the mobile media query: `.panel p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.6}` `.quote{font-size:16px!important}` `#learnedNote{font-size:11px;padding:10px}` `.panel .small{display:none}` maybe hide the long "Headphones..." paragraph on mobile? Better keep but smaller. The start button should be reachable by scrolling; that's okay.

But for a polished mobile experience, reduce. Let's add:
```
@media(max-width:760px){
 .panel{padding:22px 18px}
 .panel h1{font-size:26px;letter-spacing:.12em}
 .panel h2{font-size:9px;margin:10px 0 16px}
 .panel p{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;margin:7px 0}
 .quote{font-size:17px!important;margin:14px 0!important}
 #learnedNote{font-size:11px;padding:10px 12px;margin:12px 0}
 .controls{font-size:11px;line-height:1.7;margin:14px 0;gap:2px 16px}
 .btn{padding:12px 30px;margin-top:14px}
 .small{font-size:10.5px}
 .overlay{padding:10px}
}
```
That should fit. Let's apply and capture mobile again.

Also mobile start screen shows scrollbar (visible). Fine.

